{"version":2,"width":120,"height":30,"timestamp":1791953123,"title":"Claude Code 2.1.299 folder-trust dialog, user picks \"No, exit\", the host PowerShell prompt is left","env":{"TERM":"xterm-256color"},"pm":{"agent":"claude","agent_version":"2.1.299","initial_status":"running","bug":"VERIFY #2b: after \"No, exit\" Claude quits, the dialog text stays above and the pane's PowerShell prints a bare prompt. The pane stays alive and reads idle, so the startup wait saw \"the gate is gone\" and released the run, which typed the task into PowerShell. Fixed by 18dbba0 (a declined gate is final, never type into the host shell) and 6118dd4 (a declined dialog ends the run); 5dbdc97 drives it from these screens.","source":["D:/pm-night/verify-r7/evidence/t2b-pane-at-card.txt (the dialog, op ea83c241, folder trust-1)","D:/pm-night/verify-r7/evidence/t2b-pane-final.txt (dialog + \"PS D:\\pm-verify2\\trust-1>\")","D:/pm-night/verify-r7/evidence/app-log-excerpt.txt (dialog up 1.23 s after dispatch)","The key presses and their times are synthetic (a person moving to \"No, exit\" and pressing Enter)."]}}
[1.23,"o","\u001b[2J\u001b[H\r\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n Accessing workspace:\r\n\r\n D:\\pm-verify2\\trust-1\r\n\r\n Quick safety check: Is this a project you created or one you trust? (Like your own code, a well-known open source\r\n project, or work from your team). If not, take a moment to review what's in this folder first.\r\n\r\n Claude Code'll be able to read, edit, and execute files here.\r\n\r\n Security guide\r\n\r\n ❯ No, exit\r\n   Yes, I trust this folder\r\n\r\n Enter to confirm · Esc to cancel"]
